{
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development hereby permitted must be begun not later than the end of three years from the date of this permission. \r\rReason: To comply with the provisions of S.51 of the Planning & Compulsory Purchase Act 2004.\r",
    "The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans:\r\rLocation Plan\rE001\rE002\rE003\rE004\rE005\rP001\rP002\rP003\rP004\rP005\rD001\rPlanning Statement \r\rReason: For the avoidance of doubt and in the interests of proper planning.\r",
    "The use of the property as a House in Multiple Occupation hereby approved shall be occupied by a maximum of 7 people at any one time acting as a single household and shall not be subdivided or occupied as self-contained units. \r\rReason: To accord with the stipulations of definition as a House of Multiple Occupation and to safeguard the residential character of the surrounding area.\r",
    "No independent cooking or laundry facilities shall be installed in any of the respective bedrooms and the communal kitchen / dining room and communal bathroom shall be retained in perpetuity.\r\r",
    "Prior to occupation, the covered and secured cycle parking, as indicated on the approved plans shall be installed and ready for use. They cycle parking shall be maintained as such thereafter.\r\rReason: To ensure the provision of cycle parking in line with the Council's adopted standards.\r",
    "The development hereby permitted shall not be occupied until waste storage and recycling facilities to satisfy the future number of occupiers on site have been provided within the development, in accordance with the Enfield's Household Recycling and Waste Planning Guidance for New Developments (February 2024). Such facilities to be retained permanently thereafter.\r\rReason: In the interests of amenity and the recycling of waste materials in support of the Borough's waste reduction targets.\r",
    "No structure or erection exceeding 0.6 metres in height shall be placed within 2 metres from either side of the access point.\r\rReason: To safeguard vulnerable road users including pedestrians and to ensure vehicles are able to see the whole footway clearly when exiting the premises having regard to the more intensive use proposed.\r",
    "The development hereby permitted shall not be occupied until a Certificate of Compliance in accordance with Secured by Design Homes Guide 2024 (or the relevant Secure by Design Guide(s) or an achieved Crime Prevention Standard) has been submitted to, and approved in writing by, the Local Planning Authority. The approved details shall thereafter be installed and permanently retained.\r\rReason: In the interest of creating safer, sustainable communities.\r"
  ],
